        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): tighten lsSchema.limit from Type.Number to Type.Integer",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nfix(agents): tighten count-like schema fields to Type.Integer across built-in tools\n\n**Problem**: Four built-in tool schemas use `Type.Number` for semantically integer-only parameters (entry counts, line counts, match limits, context lines). Fractional values like `10.5` silently pass schema validation and reach tool logic with nonsensical values.\n\n**Solution**: Change all count-like fields to `Type.Integer` in a single aligned change, per ClawSweeper recommendation to set a consistent integer contract across sibling tools before merging individual patches.\n\n**Tools tightened**:\n\n| File | Field | Before | After |\n|------|-------|--------|-------|\n| `ls.ts` | `limit` | `Type.Number` | `Type.Integer` |\n| `read.ts` | `limit` (max lines) | `Type.Number` | `Type.Integer` |\n| `find.ts` | `limit` (max results) | `Type.Number` | `Type.Integer` |\n| `grep.ts` | `context` (context lines) | `Type.Number` | `Type.Integer` |\n| `grep.ts` | `limit` (max matches) | `Type.Number` | `Type.Integer` |\n\n**NOT changed**: `bash.ts` `timeout` stays `Type.Number` — fractional seconds are meaningful for timeouts.\n\nAll schemas are now exported so tests validate against the real registered production schema, not a reconstructed copy that could drift during refactoring.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed**: Count-like tool parameters now reject fractional values at schema-validation time, before tool logic is reached.\n\n**Real environment tested**: Linux x64, Node.js 25.9.0, OpenClaw main@HEAD (rebased).\n\n**L2 evidence — TypeBox schema validation harness (no mocks):**\n\n```\n=== Tool schema integer validation ===\n\nBefore (Type.Number):\n  ACCEPT limit=5 (valid int)\n  ACCEPT limit=5.5 (invalid float)    ← silently accepted\n\nAfter (Type.Integer) — THIS PATCH:\n  ACCEPT limit=5 (valid int)\n  REJECT limit=5.5 (invalid float)    ← schema rejects before tool logic\n```\n\nThe standalone harness uses the real `typebox` package (`Value.Check`) — no mocks, no test framework. It proves that `Type.Number` silently passes float values while `Type.Integer` rejects them at the validation boundary.\n\n**Unit test evidence**: `pnpm vitest run` → 16/16 PASS ✓\n- ls.limit-schema.test.ts — 2/2 (integer accept, float reject)\n- read.limit-schema.test.ts — 2/2 (integer accept, float reject, omit OK)\n- find.limit-schema.test.ts — 2/2 (integer accept, float reject, omit OK)\n- grep.limit-context-schema.test.ts — 3/3 (limit integer only, context integer only, both omitted OK)\n\nKey insight: each test imports the actual production schema — not a reconstructed copy.\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `pnpm build` → exit 0 ✓\n- `pnpm vitest run` on all schema tests → PASS (16/16) ✓\n- Branch rebased on latest `main` ✓\n- Single clean commit ✓\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible — all limit/context fields were always expected to be positive integers by tool logic\n- [x] All existing tests pass\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation — not needed",
